response:
The report describes cyberattacks targeting Ukrainian military personnel using the Signal messaging application to distribute malicious Android APK files masquerading as legitimate military software systems GRISELDA and Ochi. The fake Griselda APK delivered HYDRA malware to steal session tokens, credentials, and contacts. The trojanized Ochi APK (1.9.4.apk) contained added Java code (Crew.java, LocationEntity.java) to harvest user credentials and GPS coordinates. CERT-UA tracked the activity modifying the Ochi app under the identifier UAC-0210, assisted by military units (A0334, MILCERT), Google Cloud, and Cloudflare.

